# Every .env variant, not just `.env`. The bare pattern left `.env.bak-*`,
# `.env.prod` and anything else a hand-rolled backup is called one `git add -A`
# away from being committed — and a credential that reaches a commit is a
# rotation, not a revert (SERV-31). The examples are opted back in explicitly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.dev.example
ollama/
webui/

copyparty/

# Ansible
ansible/inventory.ini
ansible/secrets.yml
*.retry
*.log

# Secrets / env snapshots
*.snapshot
creds/

# WIP services (not yet landed as their own PRs)
services/argosy-acquisition/
services/argosy-derrick/

# System
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/

# PR reviewer scratch, written into the workspace by the reusable reviewer
# workflow and by the reviewer itself. Ignored so a reviewer running
# `git status` sees a clean tree and does not mistake its own scratch for part
# of the diff under review.
.review-scope/
review-verdict.json
review-body.md
ticket-comment.md

# Compiled Go binaries from a local `go build` in a service or module directory.
# The guard is built into an image, never committed (SERV-131 nearly committed 9MB of it).
/services/cf-access-guard/cf-access-guard
